Notes on how the checks are grounded:

- **R1/R14** — fill with 8 same-tag entries and with a 3+5 mixed distribution; `empty_o`/`full_o` compared against the model count after every committed operation.
- **R2/R8/R9/R10** — a single reference queue of `(tag, payload)` records; every completing pop compares `pop_data_valid_o` and (when valid) `pop_data_o` against the oldest model entry for that tag. Peeks (`pop_en_i=0`) leave the model untouched, so a wrongly removed/kept entry surfaces on the next pop of that tag.
- **R5** — with the store full, `push_req_i` is held for 16 cycles and any grant is a failure.
- **R11–R13** — expected hit computed by applying the masked comparison over all model entries; the all-zero mask case falls out naturally (hit iff non-empty).
- **R15** — reset asserted mid-test with entries present; store must report empty afterwards.
- **R6** — no check ever *requires* a grant merely because space exists; requests are simply held (bounded by a 200-cycle timeout that fails and `$finish`es, so a design that never grants cannot stall the run — the watchdog backs this up).
- Timing discipline: all stimulus changes at negedge, all sampling of grants/outputs just after posedge, so nothing races the sampling edge.

